onging","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Annual event; check the official page for the current date and participating organizations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uiuc-block-i-card-stunts","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Block I halftime card stunts","title":"The Block I flips its cards","subtitle":"Illinois football student section","notes":"At a home football game, watch the student section’s coordinated halftime card display and learn the design only through official game-day participation instructions.","short_summary":"A century-old Illinois student-section tradition known for orange-and-blue card displays.","evidence_claim":"The University Library documents Block I as an Illinois tradition begun in 1910, with orange and blue cards introduced in 1926.","source_url":"https://www.library.illinois.edu/slc/2025/04/14/more-than-just-a-cheering-section-the-block-i/","source_title":"More than Just a Cheering Section: The Block I","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-04-14","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Requires attendance at an applicable home football game; follow stadium and student-section rules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uiuc-orange-krush","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Orange Krush","title":"Orange Krush’s charity-and-cheering role","subtitle":"Illinois basketball student section","notes":"Look for Orange Krush at Illinois home basketball games and consult its current official participation information if you want to join its charitable efforts.","short_summary":"The basketball student section combines game support with charitable fundraising.","evidence_claim":"Illinois Admissions describes Orange Krush as part of Illinois home-court support that also raises money for local charities and organizations.","source_url":"https://www.admissions.illinois.edu/discover/campus-life/traditions","source_title":"Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Game participation and membership details vary; verify current athletics and student-section guidance.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uiuc-three-in-one","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Marching Illini Three-In-One","title":"Stand and sway for Three-In-One","subtitle":"Traditional Marching Illini halftime performance","notes":"When Three-In-One is performed, listen for its three linked songs and join the audience only as comfortably and respectfully as you choose during the halftime presentation.","short_summary":"A three-song Marching Illini halftime tradition with audience singing and swaying.","evidence_claim":"The University Library identifies Three-In-One as a traditional Marching Illini halftime performance of “The Pride of the Illini,” “The March of the Illini,” and “Hail to the Orange.”","source_url":"https://omeka-s.library.illinois.edu/s/MPAL/page/marching-illini-songs","source_title":"Marching Illini Songs","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Presented at applicable athletics events; confirm current band and game programming.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uiuc-campus-squirrels","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Campus squirrel lore","title":"The squirrels have a campus origin story","subtitle":"University grounds","notes":"Notice the campus squirrels from a respectful distance and do not feed or handle them; Illinois traces their arrival to a 1901 request by President Draper.","short_summary":"A long-lived campus fixture with a documented origin story.","evidence_claim":"Illinois Admissions states that squirrels were first brought to campus in 1901 at President Andrew S. Draper’s request.","source_url":"https://www.admissions.illinois.edu/discover/campus-life/traditions","source_title":"Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Observe wildlife from a distance; do not feed or approach animals.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
